A||||11||GT Bastard||Escort GT= Racecar? ||||13||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||12-29-2000||08:33 AM||||A friend of mine is a mechanic on the side, and he just put a new motor in a 94ish Escort GT w/5sp and got the crazy idea that it's fast(it's his car now.)  Sure, it'll do insane burnouts all through 1st, 2nd, and part of third gear, but he gets NO traction.  So I told him that I don't believe in Escorts and he starts blabbering about how it kept up with a VR6 Jetta on 3 cylinders.  That's it, we need to race!  So it's close the midnight, and the only dry stretch of road runs under a tunnel on 57th street(always deserted late at night.) We first dropped by my apartment so I could switch from my girlfriends '85 V6 to my '86 Fiero(I hadn't been driving it.) We drove out to the tunnnel, lined up, and he told me to start us.  So I say "GO" and wait for his front tire to start spinning before launching myself(I thought he could use a head start.)  Dumped the clutch at 1800rpm and burned through 1/2 of first gear(usually hook up, but pavement was cold!) As soon as I hit second gear, he was quickly falling behind.  By the end of the tunnel, he was so far back that he let off.  His sister was in the car(I had a passenger too) and she told him: "Well I guess it's not a Fiero."  She was reffering to the Escort.  Anyhow... Bwahahhaaha! And that's the story of the little Escort GT that COULDN'T.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by GT Bastard (edited 12-29-2000).]||||reg||13
Z||000001||1FST2M6||12-29-2000||08:54 AM||||Brad i assume? hehehe Show em whos really on top! Give em hell!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  LMAO!! I love it! knocking motor.. cold tires.. frozen tundra and you still wiped the floor with him! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaun41178||12-29-2000||03:15 PM||||HAHAHA I think it is hilarious when people with little 1.9 liters who can spin their tires think their car is fast.  Man you humiliated that guy!!  HAHA.  Must be nice to have a little tunnel there in your town where the road stays dry.  Not much racing here in Toledo when it has been snowing everyday at least an inch or two.  How much today?  They say 6 inches.  Man I can't wait to get back down to Daytona Beach.  I do like the wet and snow for one thing though. I live on a dead end street with a culdesack(sp?) at the end of it.  Nice big turn around area and I love to do donuts.  It is awesome as I dont  have to worry about running into anything.  Oh and I also like to get sideways like a 4 wheel slide going around turns when traffic is light and then turn into the slide and lay my foot to the floor and power out of it.  That is so much fun!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Hey Trav throw some ballast in your car to give it some weight so when I swing by it will be a bit more even.  You are going down Bro!!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
